I think it looks cute too.
我也觉得这看起来很可爱。

632
00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:43.040
All right.
好吧。

633
00:27:44.040 --> 00:27:45.600
Time for the Amper Show.
安珀秀时间到了。

634
00:27:45.600 --> 00:27:46.200
I know.
我知道。

635
00:27:46.540 --> 00:27:52.240
That's my, another one of the characters I can do for any of the voiceover folks listening.
那是我的，我能为任何收听节目的配音人士表演的另一个角色。

636
00:27:52.580 --> 00:27:54.080
Can you sustain that?
你能保持这个状态吗？

637
00:27:54.500 --> 00:27:55.580
Sure I can.
当然可以。

638
00:27:55.720 --> 00:27:56.560
Oh, you can.
哦，你可以。

639
00:27:56.740 --> 00:27:57.620
You really can.
你真的可以。

640
00:27:57.780 --> 00:27:58.560
Hey, Ange.
嘿，安吉。

641
00:27:58.780 --> 00:28:01.500
I mean, write the show for her, please.
我是说，请为她写个剧本吧。

642
00:28:02.160 --> 00:28:02.580
All right.
好吧。

643
00:28:02.880 --> 00:28:08.440
For real, we open with Nellie in the conference room with Erin and Pete.
说真的，开场是奈莉在会议室里和艾琳还有皮特在一起。

644
00:28:08.440 --> 00:28:15.640
Yeah, apparently Erin and Pete are part of this social media initiative that Nellie has set up.
是啊，显然艾琳和皮特参与了奈莉发起的这个社交媒体计划。

645
00:28:15.700 --> 00:28:19.220
So they're trying to have an online presence for Dunder Mifflin.
所以他们正试图为邓德·米夫林公司建立在线形象。

646
00:28:19.400 --> 00:28:19.620
Yeah.
是啊。

647
00:28:19.780 --> 00:28:24.100
They've created a fake profile for a really cool guy named Derek McBlack.
他们为一个叫德里克·麦克布莱克的酷哥创建了一个虚假个人资料。

648
00:28:24.500 --> 00:28:26.620
And I guess it's just Pete in sunglasses.
我想那其实就是戴着墨镜的皮特。

649
00:28:27.060 --> 00:28:32.940
And they're trying to get likes and followers and they're creating fake accounts to get those.
他们正试图获得点赞和关注，还为此创建了虚假账号。

650
00:28:32.940 --> 00:28:38.040
And at the same time, they're just being flirty and super cute.
与此同时，他们还在打情骂俏，超级可爱。

651
00:28:38.260 --> 00:28:42.120
And Nellie says, I consider myself a genius for putting the two of them together.
内莉说，我觉得自己真是个天才，把他们俩凑到了一起。

652
00:28:42.400 --> 00:28:49.620
First of all, I just want to say kudos to our writers for making Nellie's job a job.
首先，我得夸夸我们的编剧，居然能把内莉的工作安排得有模有样。

653
00:28:49.980 --> 00:28:50.460
Right.
没错。

654
00:28:50.460 --> 00:28:53.140
She really does have special projects.
她确实负责一些特别项目。

655
00:28:53.620 --> 00:28:56.600
Now, do we need these special projects?
那么，我们需要这些特别项目吗？

656
00:28:57.100 --> 00:28:57.280
Right.
并不需要。

657
00:28:57.440 --> 00:28:58.360
Probably not.
大概不需要。

658
00:28:58.580 --> 00:28:58.760
Right.
没错。

659
00:28:58.780 --> 00:29:02.540
But, you know, the social media initiative, special projects.
但你知道，社交媒体计划，特别项目嘛。

660
00:29:03.180 --> 00:29:04.080
Makes it legitimate.
这样显得名正言顺。

661
00:29:04.420 --> 00:29:05.060
All right.
好吧。

662
00:29:05.120 --> 00:29:06.660
We had a fan question from Chris W.
我们收到了一位粉丝克里斯·W的提问。

663
00:29:07.080 --> 00:29:09.080
from the New Forest, England.
他来自英国的新森林。

664
00:29:09.420 --> 00:29:15.560
When Erin and Pete are working on their grand social media initiative, they set up a fake profile for Derek McBlack.
当艾琳和皮特在进行他们宏大的社交媒体计划时，他们为德里克·麦克布莱克建立了一个虚假档案。

665
00:29:16.100 --> 00:29:20.180
Erin informs Nellie that Derek is, in fact, just Pete in sunglasses.
艾琳告诉内莉，德里克其实就是戴着墨镜的皮特。

666
00:29:20.720 --> 00:29:26.620
We only get a brief glimpse of McBlack, but I'm not convinced this is Pete in sunglasses.
我们只瞥见了麦克布莱克一眼，但我并不确信那就是戴着墨镜的皮特。

667
00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:30.320
Would the real Derek McBlack please stand up?
真正的德里克·麦克布莱克能站出来吗？

668
00:29:30.320 --> 00:29:32.540
I didn't think it looked like Pete either.
我也觉得那看起来不像皮特。

669
00:29:33.400 --> 00:29:34.260
Me either.
我也这么觉得。

670
00:29:34.860 --> 00:29:39.740
I reached out to Steve Burgess, and Steve said, Chris, you're right.
我联系了史蒂夫·伯吉斯，史蒂夫说，克里斯，你说得对。

671
00:29:39.840 --> 00:29:41.600
That doesn't look like Jake.
那看起来不像杰克。

672
00:29:44.180 --> 00:29:46.720
Steve said, I don't have any info.
史蒂夫说，我没有任何相关信息。

673
00:29:46.720 --> 00:29:50.400
I'm pretty sure we didn't ever take a picture of Jake.
我很确定我们从来没给杰克拍过那张照片。

674
00:29:50.400 --> 00:29:55.260
My guess is it's a stock photo that the art department picked of a guy in sunglasses.
我猜那是美术部门随便找的一张戴墨镜男人的库存照片。

675
00:29:55.960 --> 00:29:56.960
Good catch, Chris.
观察得很仔细，克里斯。

676
00:29:56.960 --> 00:29:57.480
I totally agree.
我完全同意。

677
00:29:57.660 --> 00:29:57.800
Yeah.
是啊。

678
00:29:58.180 --> 00:30:00.140
Here's one little catch in this scene.
这一幕里有个小细节。

679
00:30:00.300 --> 00:30:02.820
Did anyone else notice that Jake Lacey has a cold?
还有人注意到杰克·莱西感冒了吗？

680
00:30:03.460 --> 00:30:04.340
I didn't.
我没注意到。

681
00:30:04.520 --> 00:30:04.740
Yeah.
是啊。

682
00:30:04.840 --> 00:30:06.100
He has a cold in this episode.
他在这一集里感冒了。

683
00:30:06.220 --> 00:30:06.960
How do you know?
你怎么知道的？

684
00:30:07.120 --> 00:30:07.720
For sure.
非常确定。

685
00:30:08.080 --> 00:30:09.500
He's like, yeah, exactly.
他当时说，没错，就是这样。

686
00:30:09.800 --> 00:30:11.780
He's like, this is my cold.
他当时说，这就是我的感冒嗓。

687
00:30:11.920 --> 00:30:12.740
That's what he sounds like.
他听起来就是那样。

688
00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:14.400
He's like, come on, guys.
他当时说，拜托了，伙计们。

689
00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:17.420
He literally says that in the conference room later.
他后来在会议室里确实说了这句话。

690
00:30:17.600 --> 00:30:18.340
He's like, come on, guys.
他当时说，拜托了，伙计们。

691
00:30:18.340 --> 00:30:19.200
What's this all about?
这到底是怎么回事？

692
00:30:19.780 --> 00:30:26.320
I did not notice this, but I just want to say, you can do person with cold voiceover.
我没注意到，但我只想说，你可以去配感冒患者的旁白了。

693
00:30:26.360 --> 00:30:26.880
Thank you.
谢谢。

694
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:27.860
Put it on my resume.
把它写进我的简历里。

695
00:30:28.060 --> 00:30:28.220
Yep.
没错。

696
00:30:28.920 --> 00:30:33.360
Erin's going to have a talking head where she's giddy about getting to work with Pete.
艾琳有一个采访镜头，她对能和皮特一起工作感到非常兴奋。

697
00:30:33.600 --> 00:30:37.480
She talks about how well they work together, and she gets all flustered.
她谈到他们合作得有多默契，然后变得非常慌乱。

698
00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:38.340
Yeah.
是啊。

699
00:30:38.580 --> 00:30:39.020
Yeah.
是啊。

700
00:30:39.020 --> 00:30:40.440
She's clearly sweet on him.
她显然是看上他了。

701
00:30:40.560 --> 00:30:40.720
Yeah.
是啊。

702
00:30:40.780 --> 00:30:46.520
She's like, you know, I mean, I probably work well with a girl or a guy or someone I'm into.
她大概是觉得，我是说，我可能跟女生、男生或者我感兴趣的人都能合作得很好。

703
00:30:46.620 --> 00:30:47.360
Not that I'm into Pete.
并不是说我对皮特感兴趣。

704
00:30:47.360 --> 00:30:47.700
Ah!
啊！

705
00:30:48.120 --> 00:30:48.500
Yes.
没错。

706
00:30:48.860 --> 00:30:49.960
She's very cute in it.
她在里面很可爱。

707
00:30:50.220 --> 00:30:52.400
Next up, we see Jim at Athlead.
接下来，我们看到吉姆在Athlead公司。

708
00:30:52.640 --> 00:30:58.600
We find out that one of their biggest investors has requested a lunch meeting, and he just says,
我们发现他们最大的投资者之一要求共进午餐，而他只是说，

709
00:30:58.660 --> 00:31:00.520
hey, guys, is it cool if we just do it a little early?
嘿，伙计们，我们稍微提前一点行吗？

710
00:31:00.540 --> 00:31:02.640
Because remember, I have to get back to Scranton today.
因为记得吗，我今天得赶回斯克兰顿。

711
00:31:03.100 --> 00:31:04.080
And they're like, sure.
他们就说，当然可以。

712
00:31:04.200 --> 00:31:04.800
Yeah, no problem.
没问题。

713
00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:05.160
Yeah.
是啊。

714
00:31:05.500 --> 00:31:07.060
And then Jim has his talking head.
然后吉姆进行了个人访谈。

715
00:31:07.200 --> 00:31:09.680
He's very excited about Cece's ballet recital.
他非常期待西西的芭蕾舞表演。

716
00:31:10.060 --> 00:31:14.620
He's taught her a signature move, the Cece spin and kiss, and he demonstrates it.
他教了她一个招牌动作，西西旋转加飞吻，他还演示了一遍。

717
00:31:14.620 --> 00:31:16.060
He's a very cute dad moment.
这是一个非常可爱的爸爸时刻。

718
00:31:16.940 --> 00:31:21.860
I absolutely love the guy who is walking in the background of this talking head.
我超级喜欢这个访谈背景里走过的那个人。

719
00:31:22.100 --> 00:31:22.340
Oh, no.
噢，不。

720
00:31:22.700 --> 00:31:23.760
Did you see him?
你看到他了吗？

721
00:31:23.880 --> 00:31:25.200
I watched it three times.
我看了三遍。

722
00:31:25.340 --> 00:31:26.400
No, I didn't see him.
不，我没看到他。

723
00:31:26.400 --> 00:31:27.300
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

724
00:31:27.400 --> 00:31:29.300
It's such good background acting.
那背景表演得太棒了。

725
00:31:29.300 --> 00:31:41.860
He's walking by, and Jim does the spin and the kiss, and he just kind of looks in to the conference room as you would if someone was spinning and whatever for a camera.
他走过去的时候，吉姆正在做旋转和飞吻，他就像普通人看到有人在镜头前旋转表演时那样，往会议室里看了一眼。

726
00:31:42.140 --> 00:31:43.860
It's very good job.
演得真好。

727
00:31:44.180 --> 00:31:46.820
Very, very good job to the person who did this cross.
给这位路人演员点个大大的赞。

728
00:31:47.360 --> 00:31:49.820
Well, now we're going to set up a Daryl Dwight storyline.
好了，现在我们要引出达里尔和德怀特的剧情线了。

729
00:31:50.160 --> 00:31:51.740
Daryl arrives to Dunder Mifflin.
达里尔来到了邓德·米福林公司。

730
00:31:51.740 --> 00:31:56.140
And he has an athlete bag, and Dwight immediately is like, why do you have that?
他背着一个运动包，德怀特立刻就问，你为什么背着那个？

731
00:31:56.280 --> 00:31:56.660
Why are you?
你这是干什么？

732
00:31:56.760 --> 00:31:59.360
And he calls the company Stumpany, a.k.a.
他还把那家公司叫作“蠢公司”，也就是，

733
00:31:59.540 --> 00:32:00.160
Stupid Company.
愚蠢的公司。

734
00:32:00.360 --> 00:32:01.220
That really made me laugh.
那真的把我逗笑了。

735
00:32:01.360 --> 00:32:02.340
It made me laugh, too.
我也被逗笑了。

736
00:32:03.140 --> 00:32:06.000
This is when Daryl tells Dwight that he's going to work for Stumpany.
就在这时，达里尔告诉德怀特他要去“蠢公司”工作了。

737
00:32:06.440 --> 00:32:06.720
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

738
00:32:06.940 --> 00:32:08.100
Dwight is shocked.
德怀特惊呆了。

739
00:32:08.280 --> 00:32:09.120
He's so mad.
他气坏了。

740
00:32:09.240 --> 00:32:09.880
He calls Jim.
他给吉姆打了电话。

741
00:32:09.880 --> 00:32:10.440
He's furious.
他怒不可遏。

742
00:32:10.600 --> 00:32:12.540
He's like, hey, Halpert, what's the big idea?
他说，嘿，哈珀特，你到底想干什么？

743
00:32:12.720 --> 00:32:13.940
First, you jump ship.
先是你跳槽了。

744
00:32:14.120 --> 00:32:15.400
Now you're stealing Daryl, too.
现在你还要把达里尔也挖走。

745
00:32:15.580 --> 00:32:16.600
When will it end?
这什么时候才是个头？

746
00:32:16.920 --> 00:32:21.100
And Jim says, we'll take your worst fear and multiply it by infinity.
吉姆说，我们会把你最恐惧的事乘以无穷大。

747
00:32:21.740 --> 00:32:24.160
Dwight says, you won't stop until you've poached us all.
德怀特说，你们不把我们全挖走是不会罢休的。

748
00:32:24.340 --> 00:32:26.360
And Jim goes, yeah, even you.
吉姆回道，没错，连你也不放过。

749
00:32:26.520 --> 00:32:29.480
And then here's one of my favorite lines from the whole entire episode.
接下来是整集里我最喜欢的台词之一。

750
00:32:29.640 --> 00:32:33.540
Dwight says, no, I'll be damned if I'm going to let us lose me.
德怀特说，不，我绝不会眼睁睁看着我们失去我。

751
00:32:33.860 --> 00:32:34.540
I know.
我知道。

752
00:32:35.320 --> 00:32:36.940
That made me laugh so hard.
那真的把我逗乐了。

753
00:32:38.100 --> 00:32:43.160
Well, now Pam is going to approach accounting because she needs to ask Angela if she's heard
好了，现在帕姆要去找会计部，因为她需要问安吉拉是否听说了

754
00:32:43.160 --> 00:32:46.180
anything about the Irish American Cultural Center mural.
关于爱尔兰裔美国人文化中心壁画的事。

755
00:32:46.640 --> 00:32:47.940
Guess what, guys?
猜猜怎么着，伙计们？

756
00:32:47.940 --> 00:32:55.520
Guys, Angela's husband, the senator, recommended Pam to be the artist for this big mural project
伙计们，安吉拉的丈夫，那位参议员，推荐帕姆担任这个大型壁画项目的艺术家，

757
00:32:55.520 --> 00:32:56.340
in Scranton.
地点在斯克兰顿。

758
00:32:56.500 --> 00:32:58.560
Yeah, I loved this callback.
没错，我很喜欢这个呼应。

759
00:32:58.900 --> 00:33:01.920
Remember, the senator had come to the office with coffee.
还记得吗，参议员曾带着咖啡来过办公室。

760
00:33:02.140 --> 00:33:02.860
During the Target.
在《目标》那一集里。

761
00:33:03.080 --> 00:33:03.740
During the Target.
在《目标》那一集里。

762
00:33:03.900 --> 00:33:05.020
It was in deleted scenes.
那是删减片段里的内容。

763
00:33:05.020 --> 00:33:10.900
And here we have this footage because the senator is looking for Angela but wants to talk to Oscar.
这里我们有这段素材，因为参议员在找安吉拉，但想和奥斯卡谈谈。

764
00:33:11.120 --> 00:33:13.260
And Daryl says, I think they're in the warehouse.
达里尔说，我想他们应该在仓库里。

765
00:33:13.980 --> 00:33:18.260
So we've got this great footage of the senator noticing Pam making her mural.
所以我们有了这段很棒的素材，参议员注意到了正在画壁画的帕姆。

766
00:33:18.640 --> 00:33:24.540
Pam has a talking head where she says, Senator Lipton, help me submit my design for a new mural
帕姆有个采访镜头，她说，利普顿参议员，帮我提交了我的设计方案，用于市中心一栋建筑的

767
00:33:24.540 --> 00:33:26.020
on a downtown building.
新壁画项目。

768
00:33:26.260 --> 00:33:27.760
And she's waiting to hear.
她正在等消息。

769
00:33:28.060 --> 00:33:29.920
You know, she's trying to downplay it.
你知道的，她试图表现得低调一点。

770
00:33:30.060 --> 00:33:32.460
She's like, I mean, there are so many people they would go with.
她说，我是说，有那么多人选，他们可能会选别人。

771
00:33:32.540 --> 00:33:36.040
Why would they go with an unknown like me when they could have a big name like Tracy Fleab?
为什么他们会选我这种无名小卒，而不选像特蕾西·弗利布这样的大牌呢？

772
00:33:36.200 --> 00:33:37.360
Oh, Tracy Fleab.
哦，特蕾西·弗利布。

773
00:33:37.820 --> 00:33:40.500
Big time mural artist in Scranton.
斯克兰顿的大牌壁画艺术家。

774
00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:41.180
Yeah.
是啊。

775
00:33:41.820 --> 00:33:45.060
I know for a fact that Greg likes funny names.
我敢肯定格雷格喜欢这种有趣的名字。

776
00:33:45.380 --> 00:33:45.700
Yeah.
没错。

777
00:33:45.700 --> 00:33:47.600
And I feel like a bunch of names were pitched.
我觉得当时提议了很多名字。

778
00:33:47.620 --> 00:33:50.040
And they loved Fleab, Tracy Fleab.
他们很喜欢弗利布，特蕾西·弗利布。

779
00:33:50.160 --> 00:33:51.920
Sorry to all the real Fleab's out there.
向所有现实中姓弗利布的人道歉。

780
00:33:52.920 --> 00:33:53.860
There are some.
确实有一些人姓这个。

781
00:33:54.100 --> 00:33:54.620
I'm sure.
我肯定。

782
00:33:54.760 --> 00:33:56.580
But it is an interesting sounding name.
但这名字听起来确实很有趣。

783
00:33:56.680 --> 00:33:57.080
It is.
确实。

784
00:33:57.280 --> 00:33:58.320
You must know that.
你肯定知道这一点。

785
00:33:58.620 --> 00:33:58.920
Yes.
是的。

786
00:33:58.940 --> 00:34:00.380
If your last name is Fleab.
如果你姓弗利布的话。

787
00:34:00.460 --> 00:34:00.920
You know.
你懂的。

788
00:34:01.000 --> 00:34:01.380
You know.
你懂的。

789
00:34:01.580 --> 00:34:04.720
It's like this family we knew growing up when we lived overseas.
就像我们小时候住在海外时认识的一家人。

